  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Air is pumped into and released from a pressurized chamber. After $t$ minutes, the volume of air (in cubic meters) is modeled by\n\n$$\nA(t)=-6{t}^{2}+90t+400,\\,0\\le t\\le 15.\n$$\n\nFind the exact value of the instantaneous rate of change of the air volume with respect to time when $t=7$ minutes.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change when $t=7$ minutes is\n{{field-1}} cubic meters per minute.",
  "worked_solution": "The instantaneous rate of change of the air volume at $t=7$ minutes is ${A}^{\u2032}(7).$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{d}{dt}\\,(-6{t}^{2}+90t+400) \\\\  & =-12t+90.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=7,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{\u2032}(7) & =-12(7)+90 \\\\  & =-84+90 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the air volume at $t=7$ minutes is $6$ cubic meters per minute.",
